\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Definition and frequency collapse of the zero-bias CMW. Stack~A shows $\mathrm  {CMW}_\xi \approx 5.2$ at 1~kHz, whereas Stack~B shows $\approx 2.3$ at a similar dielectric peak. With increasing frequency, the branch separation collapses while substantial permittivity remains, showing that the lost quantity is state discrimination rather than the entire dielectric response.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
